    "result_text": "Full suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe request: when `sharesHousehold` is true on owner creation, allow an owner at an address already used by a same-last-name owner, assign both a stable shared `householdId`, and return it.\n\n**Files touched (4), controller and mapper untouched:**\n\n1. **`OwnerHouseholdPolicy.java`** \u2014 the one behavioural change. The existing `rejectDuplicateHousehold` already ran in the create flow, so I extended it in place rather than adding a new call site: it now loops once and, on a household match, either throws (not sharing) or assigns `owner.setHouseholdId(...)` and returns (sharing). Added a small private `householdId(...)` helper deriving a stable id from the normalized `(lastName, address)` \u2014 deterministic, so every owner in the same household derives the identical value without mutating/saving existing records.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `household_id` column field plus getter/setter, mirroring the existing `customerCode`. MapStruct auto-maps it to the DTO by name, so no mapper edit.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema, which generates the DTO accessor so the value is returned from `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** (+ the matching `data.sql` seed inserts) \u2014 added the `household_id` column (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`, so schema comes from these scripts).\n\n**Keeping structural impact low:** all logic lives in the small, self-contained `OwnerHouseholdPolicy` (tiny `WMC_other`); the controller (large surrounding class) and mapper were left alone; and the model additions are trivial CC-1 accessors.\n\n**Design note:** `householdId` is derived deterministically from the household key rather than mutating the pre-existing owner, so owners `b` and `c` in the test independently compute the same stable id \u2014 no extra saves and no reliance on ordering.\n\nResult: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
